  "slug": "dark-4pcf-cb95",
  "summary": "New hybrid EFT models, marked statistics and light-cone systematics studies target DESI, Euclid, LSST and Simons Observatory analyses beyond the power spectrum.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the modelling of tracer bias and non-Gaussian information for upcoming large-scale-structure analyses. Hybrid Lagrangian bias expansions are extended to post-reconstruction clustering, where a joint pre- and post-reconstruction analysis improves cosmological constraints. They are also extended to diffuse baryons via N-body displacements, a Lorentzian feedback suppression and linear bias. On primordial non-Gaussianity, a subhalo abundance matching model fit to small-scale clustering, combined with separate-universe simulations, constrains b_φ. Separately, neglecting light-cone and relativistic effects biases local fNL by ~2σ for a Euclid-like survey and by >10σ for a MegaMapper-like survey. Marked statistics appear in two forms: luminosity-weighted marks as a null test for assembly bias in DESI-BGS mocks, and rotation-equivariant neural marks that extract information beyond the power spectrum. Other contributions include CosmoMap, a 3D U-Net mapping dark matter to gas temperature and electron density, and lensing ratios as geometric probes of dark energy and curvature for LSST and Simons Observatory.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
